From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Widen the native mesh experiment

native_mesh gains modes 2 (multiple object workgroups), 3 (a research
state model, not qualified) and 4 (only the 31 native-index classes
Honeykrisp was qualified with), and T32 mesh state next to T16. The mode
can change at runtime through debugfs asahi_m4/native_mesh; each VM
keeps the mode it was created with, for its support header and every
decode. The GPU device advertises the current mode in sysfs
asahi_native_mesh. With a mode set, a render whose first command word is
an ordinary header is published without waiting for its producers.

The default stays 0, which leaves ordinary renders unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Cody Ho <codyho@stanford.edu>
Assisted-By: LLM
[Youwes09: Split from Gravity's "apple: integrate shared G16C and G17P GPU
on Linux 7.3" (ed2c67a9f6d4), keeping only the asahi_m4 mesh changes;
left out Gravity's own Rust API adapters.]
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
